arashtra, western India, built in 1656 on the orders of Shivaji to guard the passes of the Western Ghats.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/pratapsinh-gaekwad"><span class="enc-name">Pratapsinh Gaekwad</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pratapsinh Gaekwad was the last ruling Maharaja of Baroda, succeeding his grandfather Sayajirao Gaekwad III in 1939.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/pratinas"><span class="enc-name">Pratinas</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pratinas of Phlius was a Greek dramatist and lyric poet active in Athens around 500 BCE, when he competed against Aeschylus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/prato-cathedral"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/prato-cathedral.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Prato Cathedral</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Prato Cathedral, dedicated to Santo Stefano, grew from the parish church around which the town developed and was enlarged from the 12th to the 15th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/prattigau"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/prattigau.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Prättigau</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Prättigau is an Alpine valley of the Landquart river in the canton of Graubünden, eastern Switzerland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/pravahana-jaivali"><span class="enc-name">Pravahana Jaivali</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pravahana Jaivali was a king of Panchala who appears in the Chandogya and Brihadaranyaka Upanishads.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pravarapura"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/prava